---
import AsterLayout from "../../layouts/AsterLayout.astro";
import { ASTER_DEX_ID, AUTHORS, PERSON_ID, SITE_URL } from "../../entity";
import { buildAsterPageGraph, buildBreadcrumbs } from "../../lib/schema";
import { ASTER_DOCS, ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED } from "../../data/aster";

const url = `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/privacy/`;
const description =
  "How Aster's Account Privacy works: ZK-verifiable encrypted orders, stealth addresses, the viewer pass, and the trade-offs that come with them.";

const articleNode = {
  "@type": "TechArticle",
  "@id": `${url}#article`,
  headline: "How privacy works on Aster",
  alternativeHeadline: "How privacy works on Aster DEX",
  name: "How privacy works on Aster DEX",
  description,
  url,
  mainEntityOfPage: url,
  inLanguage: "en",
  datePublished: "2026-11-24",
  dateModified: ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED,
  author: { "@id": AUTHORS.kirsty.id },
  editor: { "@id": AUTHORS.maksim.id },
  publisher: { "@id": PERSON_ID },
  isPartOf: { "@id": `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/#collection` },
  articleSection: "Privacy",
  about: [
    { "@id": ASTER_DEX_ID },
    { "@type": "Thing", name: "Zero-knowledge proof", sameAs: "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q191943" },
    { "@type": "Thing", name: "Privacy" },
  ],
  citation: [
    { "@type": "CreativeWork", name: "Aster Chain overview", url: `${ASTER_DOCS}aster-chain/overview` },
    { "@type": "CreativeWork", name: "What is Aster?", url: `${ASTER_DOCS}overview/what-is-aster` },
  ],
};

const breadcrumbs = buildBreadcrumbs(`${url}#breadcrumbs`, [
  { name: "Home", url: `${SITE_URL}/` },
  { name: "Aster DEX", url: `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/` },
  { name: "Privacy", url },
]);

const graph = buildAsterPageGraph([articleNode, breadcrumbs]);
---

<AsterLayout
  title="How Privacy Works on Aster DEX — ZK Orders and Stealth Addresses | Maksim Sokal"
  description={description}
  canonical={url}
  graph={graph}
  trail={[{ label: "Privacy" }]}
  modified={new Date(ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED)}
>
  <header class="space-y-5 max-w-3xl">
    <span class="text-xs font-mono text-sky-400 uppercase tracking-widest block">Privacy</span>
    <h1 class="font-display font-medium text-3xl md:text-4xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight leading-tight">
      How privacy works on Aster
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      Privacy is Aster's main product claim, not a side feature. Orders are encrypted before they reach the chain,
      positions are hidden when Account Privacy is on, and each trade can settle through a one-time address. This page
      explains the mechanics and what they do not cover.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[11px] font-mono text-slate-400">
      Verified <time datetime={ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED}>{ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED}</time> ·{" "}
      <a href={`${ASTER_DOCS}aster-chain/overview`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Aster Chain overview</a>
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="problem-heading">
    <h2 id="problem-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">The problem it addresses</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      On a fully transparent perp DEX, every position size, entry and liquidation level is visible. That information has
      market value: other participants can push price toward a visible liquidation. Aster's answer is to remove the
      information from the public order flow rather than ask traders to hide it themselves.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="mechanics-heading">
    <h2 id="mechanics-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Three mechanisms</h2>
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100">1. Account Privacy</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          When enabled, asset balances and open positions are hidden from public view. When disabled, activity is
          published onchain and publicly visible. This is a per-account setting, not a global network property.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100">2. ZK-verifiable encrypted orders</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Orders are encrypted and verified with zero-knowledge proofs. The order data is never exposed onchain in
          plaintext, and trades do not appear directly in the transaction history of the primary address. Hidden orders
          require ZK verification whether Account Privacy is on or off.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100">3. Stealth addresses</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Each trade generates a fresh one-time address. A single account accumulates many ephemeral addresses, each used
          once, which breaks the link between transactions and the primary account for an outside observer.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="viewer-heading">
    <h2 id="viewer-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">The viewer pass is the trade-off</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      Privacy is not absolute. You can disclose your own history by providing a viewer pass, and verifying another
      trader's private transactions requires their pass. This is selective disclosure: useful for audits, tax reporting
      and disputes, but it means the pass is a sensitive credential. Treat it like a private key.
    </p>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
      One functional constraint is explicit in the docs: while Account Privacy is active, internal transfers to other
      users are not permitted, for regulatory reasons. If your strategy depends on moving funds between Aster accounts,
      privacy mode changes the workflow.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6" aria-labelledby="limits-heading">
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <h2 id="limits-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-lg text-slate-100 tracking-tight">What privacy covers</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <li>Balances and open positions on Aster Chain when enabled.</li>
        <li>Order contents and the link between a trade and your primary address.</li>
        <li>Your ability to prove history selectively with a viewer pass.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="font-display font-medium text-lg text-slate-100 tracking-tight">What it does not cover</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <li>The source-chain deposit transaction, which is public on the chain you deposited from.</li>
        <li>Bridge operations, which are validator-signed and verifiable onchain.</li>
        <li>Information you disclose yourself, including the viewer pass.</li>
        <li>Compliance obligations that apply to you in your jurisdiction.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-6 space-y-2" aria-labelledby="who-heading">
    <h2 id="who-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-sm text-slate-200 tracking-wide">Who benefits — and who should not rely on it</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
      Privacy helps traders who do not want their liquidation levels advertised, and funds that do not want to reveal
      strategy. It is not a substitute for legal advice, tax reporting or counterparty due diligence. If you need
      anonymity from the platform itself, this is not that product; it is privacy from public observers, with selective
      disclosure to the parties you choose.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      Related: <a href="/aster-dex/aster-chain/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Aster Chain</a> ·
      <a href="/aster-dex/shield-mode/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Shield Mode</a> ·
      <a href="/aster-dex/eligibility/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">eligibility</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-[#1e293b]/60 pt-6 space-y-3">
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      Written by <a href="/kirsty-moreland/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Kirsty Moreland</a> · Technical review by{" "}
      <a href="/about/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Maksim Sokal</a> ·
      <a href="/disclosure/" class="text-slate-400 hover:text-sky-300">Disclosure</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</AsterLayout>
